        rules: {
          objective: 'Get rid of all your cards. Last player holding cards receives a letter (P, A, or N). First to spell P-A-N loses the game.',
          gameplay: '1. **Start**: Holder of 9â™¥ plays it (and any other 9s) to start the pile. 2. **Play**: Play one card â‰¥ top, or three equal to top, or four equal higher than top. 3. **Pick up**: Take cards from pile. If >3 on 9â™¥: must take at least top 3; 9â™¥ stays. If â‰¤3 on 9â™¥: take all except 9â™¥. 4. **Turn**: When cards on pile, next player may always choose to pick up instead of playing. 5. **Out**: Players with no cards drop out. Last two: if one empties and other plays out in one turn = draw; else holder loses and gets a letter.',
          keyRules: [
            '9â™¥ always stays on table; pile builds on it.',
            'Play: 1 card â‰¥ top, or 3 = top, or 4 equal > top.',
            'Pick up: â‰¥3 cards if available, or all if â‰¤3 on 9â™¥.',
            'When only 9â™¥ on pile, next player must play (9 is lowest).',
            'Three letters P-A-N = game loser.',
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        strategy: {
          basic: 'Play high cards early to avoid picking up large piles. Save duplicates for three- or four-card plays.',
          intermediate: 'Time pickups to get useful cards. Force opponents to pick up by playing high.',
          advanced: 'Track which cards have been played; block opponents from going out.',
          tips: [
            'Playing four equal cards clears a lot of cards in one turn.',
            'Pick up when the pile has cards you need.',
            'In the endgame, holding one high card can force the opponent to pick up.',
