          ],
          deckDescription: 'A 24-card pack made by removing 2s through 8s from a standard 52-card French deck, leaving Ace, King, Queen, Jack, 10, and 9 in each suit. Used for Pan (Polish): the 9 of hearts starts the play pile; players play equal or higher or pick up; spelling P-A-N loses.',
          suitDescription: 'The four French suits (hearts, diamonds, clubs, spades) each contain six cards (A, K, Q, J, 10, 9). The 9 of hearts has a special role as the starting card; otherwise suit does not affect rank order for beating.',
          rankDescription: 'Ranks in each suit are Ace (high), King, Queen, Jack, 10, 9 (low). Players must play a card equal to or higher than the top of the pile, or pick up the pile; last player left with cards receives a letter toward P-A-N.',
